{
  "table_id": "Table_S18",
  "display_number": "S18",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S18. Comparison of baseline (2011) characteristics between participants excluded due to prevalent major chronic disease and those retained.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [
    "Note. Values are mean (SD) or n (%). Excluded participants (N = 2,471) are those removed by criterion 3 of the prespecified sequential exclusion protocol (physician-diagnosed cancer, diabetes, heart disease, stroke, chronic lung disease or memory-related disease at baseline) among biomarker-complete participants older than 45 and younger than 90 years in 2011. Included participants (N = 3,197) are the analytical baseline sample. Standardised differences are the mean difference divided by the pooled SD (continuous) or the proportion difference divided by sqrt(p(1−p)) (binary); absolute values > 0.1 indicate meaningful imbalance. Excluded participants with master-file covariates available: 2,419 (BMI) to 2,471 (age, sex); 4-year-average exposures available for 2,083. BAA is not reported for the excluded group: exclusion was driven by disease-related biomarker abnormality, so a BAA contrast would be circular; the primary-analysis BAA derivation also cannot be reproduced for participants outside the analytical sample from the delivered code. Cohort exclusion counts at each step are in Supplementary Table S4. BMI summaries exclude values outside the plausible range of 12-60 kg m⁻²."
  ],
